commit 5b8cfc2ffe05bb59fa20f912426bf27a960574d2

C03: the not-in-library consequence is not a failure for the App policy, and a licence hint is vetoed (INSTALL1623)

INSTALL1621 measured sixteen truthful Steam library finals and two remaining defects. The App's UserMessagePolicy marks «cannot» as a failure, so the English final the mind already accepted («Stardew Valley is not in your Steam library, so it cannot be downloaded or installed») was refused with reversed_result: for a verified game.entitlement.named read whose game is not the person's, that consequence is now masked (WithoutLibraryEntitlementConsequence, like the screen-reading image scope) while any other failure assertion still counts. And in one case the model added «Aunque esté en tu lista de posesiones, para instalarlo necesitas confirmarlo», hinting at a licence the read denies and at a confirmation nobody offered: the composer now vetoes such hints as extra_claim when owned is false.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


